# apps/admin local development environment.
# Copy to `apps/admin/.env.local` and adjust. Production secrets live in
# Vault / 1Password Connect — never commit real values.
#
# All four vars are required outside NODE_ENV=development|test; missing
# values crash the process at boot via `lib/env.ts` + `instrumentation.ts`
# (apps/CLAUDE.md env-var rule; CONTEXT D-05, D-06).

# There is no VITE_API_ORIGIN. The admin app calls the api via same-origin
# relative paths (/v1/*, /api/*) so the operator session cookie — host-only
# in production (07.4 D-05) — stays first-party; an absolute cross-host URL
# gets its Set-Cookie silently dropped by third-party-cookie blocking
# (Chrome, and Safari/Firefox by default for years). Dev: vite.config.ts
# proxies /api and /v1 to localhost:5001. Production: the apex's reverse
# proxy/CDN must forward /v1/* and /api/* to the api under /admin
# (10.2-17-SUMMARY.md has the full requirement).

# Apex domain the onboarding screen previews the new tenant's guest
# storefront against (07.4 D-01) — <slug>.<this> is what the restaurant's
# storefront resolves to. No scheme, no port. Dev default (localhost:3002,
# the website's dev port) is baked into `getEnv`'s `devDefaults`; only set
# this when previewing against a non-default apex.
# Production: VITE_PUBLIC_APEX_DOMAIN=restos.pp.ua
# VITE_PUBLIC_APEX_DOMAIN=localhost:3002

# Public origin of the admin web app. Forwarded as `Origin` header on
# server-side fetches so BA's trusted-origin guard passes (RES-113).
ADMIN_WEB_URL=http://localhost:4000

# Shared secret guarding `/internal/v1/*` routes. Server-only — must
# match `INTERNAL_API_TOKEN` configured for `apps/api`.
INTERNAL_API_TOKEN=internal_dev_token_change_me
